# ==============================================================================
# Two distinct concerns. Do not conflate them.
#
#   1. DUA OBLIGATION (permanent, legal)
#      Patient data and variant-level derived data must never be redistributed
#      through any channel. Enforced here, forever.
#
#   2. COMPETITIVE STRATEGY (temporary)
#      Do not reveal the causal variants while the leaderboard is open.
#      Enforced by REPOSITORY VISIBILITY, not by this file:
#
#          >>> the repository stays PRIVATE until the moment of submission <<<
#
#      The README, docs and convergence report name the causal gene. Selectively
#      redacting them would leave an incomplete artefact that reads poorly to a
#      reviewer. Visibility is the correct control.
# ==============================================================================

# ---- 1. DUA: raw patient data -----------------------------------------------
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf.gz.tbi
*.bam
*.cram
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.docx
data/
work/

# Patient HPO terms: extracted from a document marked "Do not redistribute"
patient_hpo.tsv
*phenotype*.tsv

# ---- 1b. DUA: variant-level derived data ------------------------------------
# These files list hundreds of the patient's genomic coordinates. Aggregate
# summaries (counts only) are fine; per-variant tables are not.
results/05_ranked_genes.tsv
results/05_ranking_report.txt
results/07_secondary_findings.txt
results/08_mosaic_aneuploidy.txt
results/*.html
results/*.genes.txt

# ---- Housekeeping ------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Challenge templates downloaded for reference - not our work product
docs/methods_description_form.xlsx
docs/track1_submission_template.csv

